# A build needs the Rust source, the frontend source, and the repository that stamps the version. Nothing else
# reaches the build context, so nothing else reaches the scanner.

target
gui-frontend/node_modules
gui-frontend/dist
website
# Except what the GUI builds from: the tokenizer its expression fields color code with, the language reference
# they suggest from, and the palette and controls it shares with the site.
!website/src/lib/highlight
!website/src/lib/foundry
!website/src/lib/reference.json
!website/src/lib/code-language.json
!website/src/lib/signatures.json

# This build's own output. Sending it back as context would grow with every build.
handoff

# Runtime state a checkout accumulates locally, never something an image build should ever see or embed.
smeltr-leader-data
smeltr-worker-data
smeltr-leader-secrets
smeltr.toml

*.md
docs
LICENSE*

# Except these: the export stage puts them in the handoff folder, so a site that gets the binary gets the
# terms it is licensed under and the attribution the licenses ask for with it.
!LICENSE
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
